  "rawText": "The Foundation of\n\nWIC\n\nCommunity College\n\nP.O. Box 30 + Supply, North Carolina 28462 « (919) 754-6900\n\nApril 20, i992\n\nMr. Jesse Francis\n511 North Lord Street\nSouthport, NC 28461\n\nDear Mr. Francis:\n\nOn behalf of the Brunswick Community College Foundation, I want to express cur\ndeep appreciation for your generosity in establishing the Annie E. Francis\nMemorial Endowment Scholarship. This gift of $10,000.00 has been invested, and\nthe income will be usea as a scholarship for Brunswick County residents who are\nhandicapped or dependents of a handicapped resident, who are enrolled in a two-\nyear deqree program, anc who maintain a 2.0 average.\n\nWe appreciate this endowment and the many ways you support BCC. As a loyal\nfriend, you are making a Great contribution to the College, its students, and its\nprograms. Your commitment inspires us to maintain high standards of educational\nexcellence and to seek and reward diversity among our students.\n\nWe will strive to be worthy of your confidence.\n\nYour long standing active role in educaticn is helping te build a brighter future\nin Brunswick County. Thank you again for your generous support.\n\nSincerely,\n\nGlenn M. Barefoot\nResource Development Cfficer\n|\n\nAN ENDOWMENT IN MEMORY OF AND TRIBUTE TO MY\nBELOVED WIFE OF 42 YEARS, MRS. ANNIE EVANS FRANCIS",
  "cleanedText": "The Foundation of\n\nWIC\n\nCommunity College\n\nP.O. Box 30 + Supply, North Carolina 28462 « (919) 754-6900\n\nApril 20, i992\n\nMr. Jesse Francis\n511 North Lord Street\nSouthport, NC 28461\n\nDear Mr. Francis:\n\nOn behalf of the Brunswick Community College Foundation, I want to express cur\ndeep appreciation for your generosity in establishing the Annie E. Francis\nMemorial Endowment Scholarship. This gift of $10,000.00 has been invested, and\nthe income will be usea as a scholarship for Brunswick County residents who are\nhandicapped or dependents of a handicapped resident, who are enrolled in a two-\nyear deqree program, anc who maintain a 2.0 average.\n\nWe appreciate this endowment and the many ways you support BCC. As a loyal\nfriend, you are making a Great contribution to the College, its students, and its\nprograms. Your commitment inspires us to maintain high standards of educational\nexcellence and to seek and reward diversity among our students.\n\nWe will strive to be worthy of your confidence.\n\nYour long standing active role in educaticn is helping te build a brighter future\nin Brunswick County. Thank you again for your generous support.\n\nSincerely,\n\nGlenn M. Barefoot\nResource Development Cfficer\nI\n\nAN ENDOWMENT IN MEMORY OF AND TRIBUTE TO MY\nBELOVED WIFE OF 42 YEARS, MRS. ANNIE EVANS FRANCIS",
